Percolator — vendored into Anqa
================================

Upstream:  https://github.com/aeyakovenko/percolator
License:   Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE, retained unmodified)
Vendored:  2026-07-30

WHY VENDORED RATHER THAN DEPENDED ON
------------------------------------
Two reasons.

1. We modify it. The upstream portfolio account is sized for 16 assets
   (V16_MAX_PORTFOLIO_ASSETS_N), which makes it 9,291 bytes. Anqa trades three
   assets, and every trader's portfolio is delegated into an ephemeral rollup
   where commit cost scales with account size. Reducing that capacity is a
   deliberate, load-bearing change and it belongs in this repo's history.

2. This library owns the margin arithmetic that decides who is solvent. It
   should be reviewable in the same repository as the code that calls it, not
   resolved from a remote at build time.

MODIFICATIONS FROM UPSTREAM
---------------------------
Recorded here as Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires. Any change to the account
layout must also bump V16_LAYOUT_DISCRIMINATOR and update the compile-time size
assertion, both of which upstream provides for exactly this purpose.

  2026-07-30  V16_MAX_PORTFOLIO_ASSETS_N: 16 -> 4
              V16_LAYOUT_DISCRIMINATOR:   17 -> 1017
              size assertion:             9291 -> 2859 bytes

              Rationale: the constant sizes PortfolioAccountV16Account.legs and,
              via PORTFOLIO_SOURCE_DOMAIN_CAP (= 2N), its source_domains. At 16
              the account is 9,291 bytes, ~75% of which is capacity for assets
              Anqa does not trade. Every trader's portfolio is delegated into an
              ephemeral rollup and commit cost scales with account size, so that
              capacity is a tax on every commit, per trader, forever. Anqa trades
              three assets; 4 leaves one spare slot. Result: 2,859 bytes, a 69%
              reduction.

              The layout discriminator is bumped so accounts written under the
              old shape cannot deserialize under the new one.

UPSTREAM CHARACTER
------------------
Upstream labels this "educational research project. Not production ready. Not
audited." It ships 244 Kani proofs and 51 function-contract proofs covering
no-cross-domain-value-theft, account-local safety, bounded progress and
arithmetic discipline. Those proofs are the reason it was chosen; the label is
the reason it must be audited alongside our wrapper before mainnet.
